  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Philippines: Technical Assistance to the Enabling Justice and the Rule of Law (EU GOJUST III)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To develop more coordinated, efficient, gender-sensitive, and people-centred justice services. 2) To enhance access to justice for all, especially for women and people living in vulnerable situations.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Justice sector duty bearers, such as the Judiciary, the prosecution service, law enforcement agencies, correction agencies, Katarungang Pambarangay members, the Justice Sector Coordination Council, and Justice Zones.Indirect beneficiaries: Vulnerable communities; women and girls; LGBTQI+ persons; indigenous populations; prisoners on remand and those sentenced; and the broader public.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to contribute to the Philippine socio-economic development through a more effective, inclusive, and accountable justice system.</narrative>
  </description>
